<!--
  AGENT.md — user instructions for the chat agent.

  This exact content is written automatically to config/AGENT.md on first
  boot (see api/src/config/agent-instructions.ts). config/ is gitignored —
  this committed file is the human-readable reference copy.

  Content here is appended to the system prompt after the harness's own
  tool-orchestration and behavior guidance. Use it for tone, style,
  communication preferences, or context about you — it supplements the
  harness prompt, it never overrides its tool orchestration or behavior
  rules.

  HTML comments (like this block) are stripped before the file reaches the
  model, so an unedited file behaves as "no instructions". Anything you
  write outside a comment becomes part of the prompt on the next
  POST /api/v1/settings/reload or restart.

  Example (uncomment and edit):
  Prefer concise answers. Default to metric units. Address me as "boss".
-->
